# Google Calendar scheduling (M4) is entirely client-side and gated on this OAuth Client
# ID. Without it, the Schedule panel shows a note instead of the meeting form.
#
# 1. Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application) in the Google Cloud Console.
# 2. Add authorized JavaScript origins: http://localhost:5173 and https://overlap.vercel.app
# 3. Copy this file to .env.local and paste the client id below.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# PostHog analytics. Without both of these set, PostHog is skipped (a console
# warning is logged) and no analytics events are sent.
VITE_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=

# overlap-api's base URL, e.g. http://localhost:3000 for a local `npm run dev`
# in ../overlap-api. Turns short links on: the Share button produces a path-
# based URL (overlapclock.com/abc123) instead of the #c= hash link, and a
# short-link-shaped path is resolved against GET /links/:id on load. Unset
# (the default) disables the feature entirely — the app behaves exactly as it
# does today. overlap-api's own FRONTEND_ORIGIN must also include this app's
# origin, or every request is refused by CORS. See README.md's "Short links"
# section for local setup and the production checklist.
VITE_OVERLAP_API_URL=
